And then how should it go about doing the job?

507
00:21:48.840 --> 00:21:50.575
As always, it should think carefully and

508
00:21:50.575 --> 00:21:52.344
it should use tools to perform actions.

509
00:21:52.644 --> 00:21:54.079
The first thing it should do is

510
00:21:54.079 --> 00:21:55.547
take a look at each construction rule,

511
00:21:55.947 --> 00:21:59.251
both the node construction rules
and the relationship construction rules.

512
00:21:59.551 --> 00:22:02.454
It should then use its tools to validate
that the construction rules

513
00:22:02.754 --> 00:22:05.090
are relevant and correct. And then if

514
00:22:05.090 --> 00:22:07.426
that's all passes and all looks good,

515
00:22:07.726 --> 00:22:10.629
you can respond with a single word valid.

516
00:22:10.962 --> 00:22:13.098
If the schema has any problems,

517
00:22:13.398 --> 00:22:16.001
respond with a retry and provide some feedback.

518
00:22:16.501 --> 00:22:20.038
And the feedback here is asked as a concise bullet list.

519
00:22:20.539 --> 00:22:23.842
So, if the critic has any concerns
about what's been proposed,

520
00:22:23.842 --> 00:22:25.177
we should see this nice bullet

521
00:22:25.177 --> 00:22:26.745
list explaining what changes should be made.

522
00:22:27.112 --> 00:22:29.915
That feedback will eventually be put into the loop

523
00:22:30.015 --> 00:22:32.084
and passed back to the proposal agent

524
00:22:32.184 --> 00:22:34.119
to change what it's done and try

525
00:22:34.119 --> 00:22:36.288
to take into account any of the feedback.

526
00:22:38.023 --> 00:22:40.559
You can then go ahead and combine
all those prompt parts

527
00:22:40.559 --> 00:22:43.161
into a single prompt that will be the critic agent instruction

528
00:22:43.161 --> 00:22:45.664
that we'll use for defining the agent in just a moment.

529
00:22:48.667 --> 00:22:50.669
Now, the schema critic also needs tools,

530
00:22:50.936 --> 00:22:53.638
but there aren't any tools
that are novel to the schema critic.

531
00:22:53.638 --> 00:22:56.641
It can use the same tools that the proposal agent used,

532
00:22:56.942 --> 00:22:59.144
and we're just going to include them here into a list.

533
00:22:59.644 --> 00:23:01.947
It's getting the approved user goal, the approved files,

534
00:23:02.147 --> 00:23:05.650
and then the utility tools like
sampling the file or searching files.

535
00:23:07.686 --> 00:23:10.689
You've got all the components necessary
for the critic agent,

536
00:23:10.689 --> 00:23:12.424
so you can go ahead and create the

537
00:23:12.424 --> 00:23:14.159
agent. It's going to be an LLM agent.

538
00:23:14.159 --> 00:23:17.062
Its name is going to be the schema_critic_agent_v1.

539
00:23:17.662 --> 00:23:19.364
And here's one thing that's novel about

540
00:23:19.364 --> 00:23:21.066
this agent that we haven't seen before.

541
00:23:21.666 --> 00:23:24.169
Unlike other agents that simply do their work and

542
00:23:24.169 --> 00:23:26.671
then use tools for, you know, having some output,

543
00:23:26.872 --> 00:23:29.674
this agent is simply going to respond with some text,

544
00:23:29.875 --> 00:23:33.378
and that text is going to be captured into state using this

545
00:23:33.879 --> 00:23:35.981
output key. So this output key,

546
00:23:35.981 --> 00:23:38.083
here we're calling it feedback, means that

547
00:23:38.083 --> 00:23:40.385
when this agent is done, when the final message

548
00:23:40.385 --> 00:23:42.254
from this agent has been received,

549
00:23:42.254 --> 00:23:45.657
that final message will be stored into state

550
00:23:45.657 --> 00:23:47.259
using the key feedback.

551
00:23:47.259 --> 00:23:49.661
so that state dictionary that we've got

552
00:23:49.661 --> 00:23:52.464
will have this value generated by the critic.

553
00:23:52.464 --> 00:23:54.666
Because that's there, later on,

554
00:23:54.666 --> 00:23:56.568
if you loop back to the proposer,

555
00:23:56.568 --> 00:23:58.870
the proposal will be able to get that information

556
00:23:58.870 --> 00:24:03.742
back from the state.
You've defined the two critical components,

557
00:24:03.742 --> 00:24:06.945
the two critical sub-agents within this refinement loop.

558
00:24:07.345 --> 00:24:09.347
Now we have to define the refinement loop itself.

559
00:24:10.081 --> 00:24:11.149
And just before we do that,

560
00:24:11.149 --> 00:24:12.384
there's going to be one more agent

561
00:24:12.384 --> 00:24:14.486
that's going to be a custom agent that we define.

562
00:24:15.120 --> 00:24:16.721
If we go back to the architectural diagram,

563
00:24:16.922 --> 00:24:19.124
we've got the proposal agent, the critic agent,

564
00:24:19.524 --> 00:24:22.427
and now we're going to add
this CheckStatusAndEscalate agent.

565
00:24:23.028 --> 00:24:25.130
This agent has one job,

566
00:24:25.130 --> 00:24:26.231
and its job is to decide

567
00:24:26.231 --> 00:24:27.532
whether or not the loop is done.

568
00:24:28.233 --> 00:24:29.835
Let's take a look at how this works.

569
00:24:30.535 --> 00:24:32.237
So this is a base class

570
00:24:32.237 --> 00:24:34.206
called BaseAgent that we're going to extend,

571
00:24:34.206 --> 00:24:37.509
and we're just going to call it
the CheckStatusAndEscalate class.

572
00:24:38.009 --> 00:24:39.678
This is going to be a custom

573
00:24:39.678 --> 00:24:41.313
agent with a custom run function here.

574
00:24:41.813 --> 00:24:43.515
This run function will get invoked.

575
00:24:43.515 --> 00:24:46.818
It'll get the current context in which it was being invoked,

576
00:24:46.818 --> 00:24:49.020
and we're not going to take too much concern about that,

577
00:24:49.020 --> 00:24:51.323
except for looking at the current session state.

578
00:24:51.623 --> 00:24:53.325
So from that context, we're going to look

579
00:24:53.325 --> 00:24:55.026
for the current session, look at the state,

580
00:24:55.026 --> 00:24:58.930
and we're going to get the feedback.
If there is any feedback,

581
00:24:58.930 --> 00:25:01.333
and if not, we're going to assume that the feedback is valid.

582
00:25:01.333 --> 00:25:03.702
So if there's no feedback from the critic agent,

583
00:25:03.702 --> 00:25:05.370
we're going to assume that it's valid. Or

584
00:25:05.370 --> 00:25:07.005
if the agent has said that it's valid,

585
00:25:07.005 --> 00:25:09.007
the result of this will be that the feedback is valid.

586
00:25:09.007 --> 00:25:11.009
And so this should_stop flag will be

587
00:25:11.009 --> 00:25:13.311
set based on whether or not the feedback

588
00:25:13.311 --> 00:25:15.413
has the content valid.

589
00:25:15.413 --> 00:25:18.316
It's a very simple check.
We could be more sophisticated about this,

590
00:25:18.316 --> 00:25:20.619
but this works, you know, just fine for most of the agents.

591
00:25:20.619 --> 00:25:23.622
If this is all true, we're going to yield a new event

592
00:25:23.622 --> 00:25:25.690
authored by, of course, this special

593
00:25:25.690 --> 00:25:27.659
agent that we've constructed here

594
00:25:27.859 --> 00:25:29.861
and it's going to take a very specific action.

595
00:25:30.061 --> 00:25:32.664
We're going to add an action to this event called escalate.

596
00:25:33.064 --> 00:25:36.868
And the value of escalate is going
to be based on should_stop.

597
00:25:36.968 --> 00:25:38.770
So should_stop will be true if

598
00:25:38.770 --> 00:25:40.872
the current feedback is valid or empty.

599
00:25:41.273 --> 00:25:44.075
If it's not empty, then escalate will be false,

600
00:25:44.276 --> 00:25:46.278
which means we'll still emit this event,

601
00:25:46.478 --> 00:25:49.881
but the escalation won't happen
because we said escalate equals false.

602
00:25:50.181 --> 00:25:51.883
That's enough to either break out

603
00:25:51.883 --> 00:25:53.885
of the loop or continue the loop.

604
00:25:54.519 --> 00:25:56.821
You can finally create the LoopAgent.

605
00:25:56.821 --> 00:26:01.326
The LoopAgent is a special workflow agent
that takes a list of sub_agents,

606
00:26:01.326 --> 00:26:06.326
here the schema_proposal_agent, the schema_critic_agent,
and that custom CheckStatusAndEscalate agent,

607
00:26:06.531 --> 00:26:08.333
and puts them inside of a loop.

608
00:26:08.333 --> 00:26:10.535
All this that does is no reasoning whatsoever,

609
00:26:10.535 --> 00:26:13.338
all it does is coordinate the execution of these other agents.

610
00:26:13.338 --> 00:26:15.373
And you can see there's one interesting thing

611
00:26:15.373 --> 00:26:17.442
here, it has a new parameter called max_iterations.

612
00:26:17.676 --> 00:26:19.811
and we're setting that to two,

613
00:26:19.811 --> 00:26:21.813
which means the loop will happen at most twice.

614
00:26:22.314 --> 00:26:24.182
So either we've gotten to a consensus

615
00:26:24.182 --> 00:26:26.885
and the critic has agreed that a proposal is good,

616
00:26:26.885 --> 00:26:28.753
or if not, we'll still exit this

617
00:26:28.753 --> 00:26:30.589
loop, we're not going to continue forever.

618
00:26:31.089 --> 00:26:33.191
And when this is done, the result will either be

619
00:26:33.191 --> 00:26:35.093
that we have a confirmed schema,

620
00:26:35.493 --> 00:26:36.962
or if not, that perhaps you

621
00:26:36.962 --> 00:26:38.697
need some more input from the user

622
00:26:38.697 --> 00:26:40.498
about how to actually approach the schema.

623
00:26:40.865 --> 00:26:43.368
So you can go ahead and create that agent too.

624
00:26:44.869 --> 00:26:48.073
You can finally create
an execution environment for this agent

625
00:26:48.073 --> 00:26:50.075
and then call it, passing it the

626
00:26:50.075 --> 00:26:52.344
user message, How can these files be imported?

627
00:26:52.544 --> 00:26:56.047
Now, as before, when we create this execution environment,

628
00:26:56.047 --> 00:26:58.750
we're going to initialize the state
with some feedback that is blank,

629
00:26:58.750 --> 00:27:00.952
the user goal, and the approved files.

630
00:27:01.486 --> 00:27:03.588
The agent that we're going to be running here though

631
00:27:03.588 --> 00:27:05.290
is the schema_refinement_loop.

632
00:27:05.690 --> 00:27:08.259
Into the refinement_loop_caller,
we'll pass in the user message,

633
00:27:08.660 --> 00:27:10.328
we'll wait for it to finish, get the

634
00:27:10.328 --> 00:27:11.963
session state and take a look at it.

635
00:27:13.898 --> 00:27:16.201
So you can see that this takes a little while

636
00:27:16.201 --> 00:27:17.502
because we're actually going to be both

637
00:27:17.502 --> 00:27:18.803
iterating on the loop at most twice,

638
00:27:18.803 --> 00:27:21.506
but also in order to do this evaluation,

639
00:27:21.506 --> 00:27:22.874
there's two agents that are going to

640
00:27:22.874 --> 00:27:24.209
be taking a look at the files.

641
00:27:24.209 --> 00:27:26.511
The first one, of course, the proposal agent

642
00:27:26.511 --> 00:27:27.812
is going to be looking at each

643
00:27:27.812 --> 00:27:29.080
of these files and deciding how to

644
00:27:29.114 --> 00:27:31.116
create a knowledge graph out of that.

645
00:27:31.116 --> 00:27:32.751
but then the critic is basically going

646
00:27:32.751 --> 00:27:34.619
to look at the same set of files

647
00:27:34.619 --> 00:27:37.288
and decide whether or not the proposal is valid or not.

648
00:27:37.288 --> 00:27:39.891
So you can see we started with the refinement loop,

649
00:27:39.891 --> 00:27:42.293
went on to proposal agent v1,

650
00:27:42.293 --> 00:27:44.896
then the critic finally got started.

651
00:27:45.296 --> 00:27:47.599
back to the proposal agent,

652
00:27:47.599 --> 00:27:49.601
back to the critic agent again.

653
00:27:50.101 --> 00:27:52.003
Oh, the critic is still not satisfied.

654
00:27:52.604 --> 00:27:54.506
Here the final response was that the

655
00:27:54.506 --> 00:27:56.408
critic says, no, you've got to retry.

656
00:27:56.708 --> 00:28:00.311
It's unhappy with something about what the proposal is.

657
00:28:00.612 --> 00:28:03.214
It thinks there's some overlap in relationships,

658
00:28:03.515 --> 00:28:05.316
the data maybe is not complete.

659
00:28:05.717 --> 00:28:07.819
I won't read through all the feedback here,

660
00:28:07.919 --> 00:28:09.554
but this feedback is exactly what should

661
00:28:09.554 --> 00:28:11.222
be passed back to the proposal agent

662
00:28:11.222 --> 00:28:13.124
to actually improve its results.

663
00:28:13.525 --> 00:28:17.328
So in this invocation,
even though we went through two iterations

664
00:28:17.328 --> 00:28:20.331
through the refinement loop,
the critic has not been satisfied.

665
00:28:20.532 --> 00:28:23.034
This is when in the overall architecture,

666
00:28:23.334 --> 00:28:25.437
this loop would have terminated

667
00:28:25.537 --> 00:28:28.406
and actually the overall control flow would have been passed back

668
00:28:28.406 --> 00:28:30.408
to the Schema Proposal Coordinator.

669
00:28:30.875 --> 00:28:33.078
This is the agent that actually involves a human.

670
00:28:33.078 --> 00:28:36.381
So this is where the coordinator could say to the human,

671
00:28:36.381 --> 00:28:39.684
hey, not sure about what schema to produce.
Here's what I've got.

672
00:28:39.684 --> 00:28:41.586
What do you think we should do next? Should

673
00:28:41.586 --> 00:28:43.488
we keep trying or do you have some suggestions?

674
00:28:43.988 --> 00:28:44.989
Without the human in the loop here,

675
00:28:44.989 --> 00:28:45.990
you could try to run this again.

676
00:28:45.990 --> 00:28:47.992
You could go into the notebook.

677
00:28:48.259 --> 00:28:50.762
reset these cells and try to run this again.

678
00:28:50.862 --> 00:28:54.065
You could try to refine the message that's passed in here,

679
00:28:54.165 --> 00:28:55.533
the kinds of things you would

680
00:28:55.533 --> 00:28:57.168
do if you're directly interacting with this.

681
00:28:57.635 --> 00:28:59.337
There will be an optional version of this

682
00:28:59.337 --> 00:29:01.039
where we will actually go ahead and incorporate

683
00:29:01.139 --> 00:29:02.841
this top-level coordinator

684
00:29:02.941 --> 00:29:05.410
that you'll be able to interact with and actually see how

685
00:29:05.510 --> 00:29:07.278
either through a single refinement or

686
00:29:07.278 --> 00:29:09.314
multiple refinements or some suggestions from you,

687
00:29:09.414 --> 00:29:11.716
you can get to a schema proposal

688
00:29:11.816 --> 00:29:13.718
that the critic likes, that you like,

689
00:29:13.818 --> 00:29:15.086
and that you can move forward

690
00:29:15.086 --> 00:29:16.521
with to actually construct a knowledge graph.
